# ── PROPRIETARY / CLOSED SOURCE ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The following are NOT part of the open source CLI.
# They live in private repositories.

# NOTE: docs/, scripts/ and relay/migrations/ used to be ignored here as
# "internal". They are now tracked — the schema history, the host-provisioning
# scripts and the operational runbooks are things you cannot rebuild from
# memory after a lost laptop, and keeping them out of version control was a
# bigger risk than publishing them. They contain no credentials (verified);
# every secret still lives in server-side .env files, which stay ignored below.

# Relay server binary (build artefact)
relay/server

# Freemium / internal — keep locally, do not publish
.tunr.schema.json
CODEOWNERS

# Dashboard + landing page (proprietary — not published to GitHub)
landing/

# ── SECRETS / CREDENTIALS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEVER commit these. Ever.
supabase.json
paddle.json
.env
.env.*
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.secret

# Node.js (for SDK and dashboard)
node_modules/
.next/
.vercel/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Pivot planning material — reference only, not part of the module.
# (ref/tunrpivot/*.go are stray copies whose package names collide, which
#  breaks `go build ./...` and `go test ./...` — the release gate.)
ref/
